# Masarifi Environment Configuration
# ========================================

# Supabase Sync Proxy URL (required for remote backup and sync)
VITE_PROXY_URL=http://localhost:3000/supabase

# Developer Unlock (DEVELOPMENT BUILDS ONLY — `npm run dev`)
# ----------------------------------------------------------
# These two variables drive the developer unlock dialog (tap the version number
# seven times in Settings). The feature is compiled out of production builds:
# every code path is wrapped in `import.meta.env.DEV`, which Vite replaces with
# `false` at build time so the branch — and these literals — are tree-shaken
# away. Verified by: `npx vite build && grep -r "MASTER_HASH" dist/` -> no hits.
#
# Setting them in a production .env has NO effect; the code that reads them does
# not exist in the shipped bundle. Do not attempt to re-enable this in
# production: a secret compiled into a client binary is not a secret. If remote
# support unlock is ever required, implement it as a server-issued, expiring,
# single-use token validated by the backend.
#
# Generate your own values using: node -e "require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex')"
# VITE_MASTER_HASH=<your_own_pbkdf2_hash>
# VITE_MASTER_SALT=<your_own_random_salt>

